# {{STUDIO_REPO}}

Persistent context repo for Claude sessions building **{{SYSTEM_NAME}} consumer screens + coded prototypes**
({{PROJECT_NAME}} / {{PARENT_ORG}} {{DOMAIN}}).

> **Scope: screen creation + live prototyping only.** Composing the published {{SYSTEM_NAME}} library into
> pixel-perfect consumer screens (Figma file `{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}`), the UX definition that
> precedes them (flows / IA / state matrices / specs / functional copy), and instrumented coded
> prototypes. The **design system itself** — tokens, styles, components, variants, the manifest,
> publish, drift — lives in the separate **`{{DS_REPO}}`** repo, which *publishes* {{SYSTEM_NAME}};
> this repo *consumes* it.

## Why this repo exists

Working with Claude across sessions requires re-establishing context each time: which design system,
which Figma file IDs, which conventions, which working preferences. Manual copy-paste is fragile and
grows stale. This repo solves that — a single bootstrap gives Claude everything it needs to build
screens against {{SYSTEM_NAME}}.

## How it works

1. Open this repo in **Claude Code** — it loads `CLAUDE.md` (→ `CONTEXT.md`) automatically on startup.
2. `CONTEXT.md` + `CLAUDE.md` carry the project facts, skill table, and critical rules; the `.claude/`
   **agents** (`ux-designer`, `ui-designer`, `flow-reviewer`, `consumer-migrator`, `data-analyst`) +
   **commands** (`/design-review`, `/consumer-audit`, `/rebind`, `/usability-report`) + invocable
   **skills** (`ux-flow-review`, `usability-analytics`, `rebind`) carry the workflows.
3. Load `skills/*.md` per task and delegate to the right agent. For coded prototypes, drive the
   `usability-prototype` skill. Three shared building blocks keep the system honest: **`ux-flow-review`**
   (the single heuristic-evaluation canon every review surface loads), **`usability-analytics` /
   `data-analyst`** (validates screens with behavioral DATA vs UX benchmarks, not opinion), and the
   **`rebind` / `consumer-migrator`** consume-verification loop (proves a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish is actually
   used downstream).

When {{SYSTEM_NAME}} changes, the DS context republishes and updates its skills/manifest; refresh the read-only
skill mirrors here (see *Updating the context*) and the next session builds against current {{SYSTEM_NAME}}.

