Private repo: append `?token=YOUR_PAT` (a GitHub PAT with `repo` scope) to the raw URL. Note: a
PAT-in-URL appears in chat history — for higher security use Claude Projects with manual uploads.

## Working with the prototype

Coded prototypes are the **usability-validation gate** of the pipeline: a flow is usability-tested
as an instrumented prototype (task success, time-on-task, SEQ, heatmaps) *before* it goes live or is
handed to the product team + engineers. The Figma gates prove fidelity + system compliance; the
prototype proves it works for users. A failed test routes back to design, not forward.

The **`data-analyst`** (via `/usability-report`) then turns that instrumentation into benchmarked
evidence — PostHog/Clarity/SEQ vs documented UX norms — so the `ux-designer` validates the screens on
data, not opinion. Ready-made queries live in `prototypes/{{PROTOTYPE_NAME}}/analytics-queries.md`.

```bash
cd prototypes/{{PROTOTYPE_NAME}}
npm install
npm run dev        # http://localhost:5173
npm run build      # production build
```

Analytics keys live in `prototypes/{{PROTOTYPE_NAME}}/.env` (gitignored). Copy `.env.example` → `.env` and
fill in FREE Clarity + PostHog keys; with none set the prototype still runs and logs task timings to
the on-screen HUD. `.vercel/` links the deploy and is gitignored — never commit either.

